            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous Right Coronary Artery Rupture and Acute Cardiac Tamponade in Behçet's Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e149-e151</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1443-9506(16)30232-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.hlc.2016.04.022</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary involvement in Behçet's disease is extremely rare and it can bring devastating consequences when it occurs. In this report, we present a 29-year-old male patient with Behçet's disease who developed rapidly changing and progressive coronary artery involvements under medical treatment.</AbstractText>
